Monadic devas are high level monsters that are resistant to most
low-level attacks.  They have a chance of being created with a shield
of reflection, which could be a problem if you are planning on
disintegrating it. They have a 90% chance of resisting magic attacks.

They are not stoning resistant, though.  Polymorphing into a basilisk
is a useful idea.

A quick glance at http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/slashem/ shows
that the monster with the most damaging melee attacks appears to be:
vorpal jabberwock            20d8  -2  50%  1=D7 3d10 3d10 3d10 3d10
which looks like average of 66 damage per round.

If you can get an amulet of unchanging, from a wish for example, you
might want to permanently take the form of a crystal golem.  They have
a lot of useful intrinsics, including magic resistance and reflection,
and a random breath attack.

A black dragon is also a possible choice, but you may want to find out
if the deva has reflection first.



